From eb0130c8bce11af5f26bebe45e9eed6fffbaea62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:07:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] yblod-engine-vk: narrow dual MMR variant (one pair per
 invocation)

fel_mmr_dual_horizontal (the staged Annex B FEL chroma: 174 ms of a
picture on the first Pi 5 run) worked on two pairs per invocation, keeping
two 10-sample EL windows, four results and the 64-bit MMR state live (64
registers, 2 threads on V3D). S_PIXELS (constant 27) = 2: one pair per
invocation, the EL window loaded as words and filtered at once. Used by
the specialized variant when DVVK_NARROW (default: with the portable
shaders, i.e. GPUs without shaderInt64 such as the Pi 5); the engine
dispatches by the variant in use. Peak registers 64 -> 54 (still 2
threads: the dual 64-bit MMR itself). Outputs identical, narrow or not.
---
 .../vk/shaders/fel_mmr_dual_horizontal.comp   | 71 +++++++++++++++++++
 yblod-engine/vk/src/engine.rs                 | 23 ++++--
 yblod-engine/vk/src/gpu.rs                    |  2 +
 yblod-engine/vk/src/options.rs                |  6 ++
 4 files changed, 97 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

